--- two RED-stage disclosures, recorded rather than glossed ---
  1. TEST-003's own assertions were appended to the two PRE-EXISTING ok
     conformance cases (failures 1 and 2 above). Those cases call
     assertConforms() before assertHostRequiredChecks(), so in RED the ajv
     gate fails first and TEST-003's runtime assertion is never reached in
     those two cases. TEST-003's runtime proof is therefore carried by
     failures 6/7/8, which reach assertHostRequiredChecks (or its inline
     equivalent) directly and report "hostRequiredChecks is absent". The
     same ordering situation T-001's red.log records.
  2. Two of this task's new cases are GREEN already in RED, by construction,
     and this is disclosed rather than presented as a red-to-green
     transition:
       - "TEST-009 leg (AC-009): the schema requires hostRequiredChecks and
         pins its nested shape"
       - "TEST-016 (AC-016): the schema description is verbatim
         requirements.md's CONFIRMED literal"
     Both assert the CONTENT of the schema file, and the schema file is
     precisely what RED proof (a) changes. Their red state would be "the
     schema edit was not made", which is not the state under test here.
     Their value is regression protection against a later drift of the
     schema away from requirements.md, and they are listed among the
     206 passes below, not among the 8 failures.

